WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:04.469
- It's like living with like
a leash on, a little bit.

00:00:04.469 --> 00:00:05.910
You can do some stuff,

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.883
but every now and then you
remember that it's there.

00:00:12.083 --> 00:00:14.547
- I was living in Japan
during the earhquake in 2011.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:17.214
- A few weeks and months
of political unrest

00:00:17.214 --> 00:00:18.877
while I was living overseas.

00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:20.897
We lived with bags by
the door, ready to go,

00:00:20.897 --> 00:00:22.208
in case we needed to get out.

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:25.657
- I found out in 2008 I
had PTSD, Complex PTSD,

00:00:25.657 --> 00:00:28.667
but I think the diagnosis
should have probably been made

00:00:28.667 --> 00:00:30.571
when I was 14 years old.

00:00:30.571 --> 00:00:33.834
- I was raped and as a result

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:36.610
I live with PTSD.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.100
- The civil war in
Lebanon broke out in 1975.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.310
I was only 17 years old.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.386
I lived through that for about 12 years.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.491
- As it kind of sunk in, I
started to feel really guilty,

00:00:50.001 --> 00:00:53.124
because I had always associated PTSD

00:00:53.124 --> 00:00:55.234
with people who had been to war,

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:58.082
and I just didn't think I deserved it.

00:01:02.872 --> 00:01:04.831
- The PTSD triggers, they ambush you.

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.419
You don't know when it's going to come.

00:01:06.419 --> 00:01:08.588
It's with the unknown
every day you wake up and

00:01:08.588 --> 00:01:11.902
you don't know if you are
going to have a trigger today.

00:01:11.902 --> 00:01:13.921
- I was at a movie

00:01:13.921 --> 00:01:15.814
and there's a part where

00:01:15.814 --> 00:01:18.318
this woman got trapped in a car.

00:01:18.318 --> 00:01:19.863
I had a serious panic attack.

00:01:19.863 --> 00:01:21.252
- There's a song that was talking about

00:01:21.252 --> 00:01:23.335
like, shooting and armed robbery.

00:01:23.335 --> 00:01:25.501
And just hearing that song, like,

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:26.874
that was all it took.

00:01:26.874 --> 00:01:28.839
- Something happened when I was 13

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:31.223
and when my trigger
happens, in that moment,

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.742
I am 13.

00:01:32.742 --> 00:01:35.573
- Usuallly the sounds
of jet planes overhead

00:01:35.923 --> 00:01:40.296
would trigger off the
memory for me of those days.

00:01:40.296 --> 00:01:42.845
It would make me feel weak in the legs,

00:01:42.845 --> 00:01:45.160
and my memory will go back to that time,

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.355
trying to look after my
children when they were little

00:01:47.355 --> 00:01:48.704
and protect them.

00:01:49.914 --> 00:01:52.033
All I have to do is hear a jet plane,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.161
and that's where my mind will go.

00:01:54.161 --> 00:01:57.534
- At times it has literally
felt like I'm dying.

00:01:58.564 --> 00:02:02.883
You feel like you're never
going to get past this.

00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:10.048
One of the things that's helped
me a lot was group therapy.

00:02:10.048 --> 00:02:12.300
This happens to more
people than you think.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:14.077
- I start to have a conversation

00:02:14.077 --> 00:02:16.405
with this thing that you have.

00:02:16.405 --> 00:02:18.504
- I did counseling for
two years in college.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:19.988
It felt like that got my life

00:02:19.988 --> 00:02:21.566
into a pretty manageable place.

00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:24.785
- I am trying to build up the courage

00:02:24.785 --> 00:02:26.705
to attempt a support group.

00:02:26.705 --> 00:02:29.454
- I would have these days
where you're just like,

00:02:29.454 --> 00:02:31.294
you know, there's nothing I can do

00:02:31.294 --> 00:02:33.259
to do anything that you're supposed to do.

00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:35.510
In group therapy, someone
called it a lost day.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.671
It's such a simple thing, but putting

00:02:38.061 --> 00:02:41.922
the words "lost day" to those days

00:02:41.922 --> 00:02:43.983
helped me, like, overcome.

00:02:43.983 --> 00:02:46.447
- And I think accepting
that is really important,

00:02:46.447 --> 00:02:48.451
and to just be, like, it's
OK to, like, freak out.

00:02:48.721 --> 00:02:50.594
And just be, like, this is
scary, because it's scary.

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:53.172
- And don't ever tell them to get over it,

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:56.049
because it's extremely painful.

00:03:05.229 --> 00:03:08.231
- It takes practice,
and it takes patience,

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:09.189
and it takes faith.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.385
You have to know that the fact

00:03:10.385 --> 00:03:12.556
that you've been through
something so traumatic,

00:03:12.556 --> 00:03:13.791
and you're here,

00:03:13.791 --> 00:03:16.344
you are much stronger
than you think you are.

00:03:16.344 --> 00:03:18.207
- Don't feel guilty when
you have a good day.

00:03:18.207 --> 00:03:19.749
- Give yourself time to heal.

00:03:19.749 --> 00:03:21.453
- You can't judge yourself for it.

00:03:21.453 --> 00:03:23.679
- It'll never be the same,
but it can get better.

00:03:23.679 --> 00:03:25.590
And it's worth whatever
it's going to take.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:27.038
You can have a better life.

00:03:27.038 --> 00:03:28.965
- There's light at the end of the tunnel.

00:03:28.965 --> 00:03:31.519
You've just got to find the
right thing that works for you.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:34.391
- And getting help is
not a sign of weakness.

00:03:34.391 --> 00:03:37.501
It takes a lot of strength
and a lot of courage.

00:03:38.691 --> 00:03:40.736
And you deserve the happiness

00:03:40.736 --> 00:03:42.500
that comes with getting better.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.526
- My name is Kate.

00:03:43.526 --> 00:03:44.906
- My name is Tammy.

00:03:44.906 --> 00:03:45.893
- My name is Kirk.

00:03:45.893 --> 00:03:47.653
- [All] And I live with PTSD.

